<title>RUSSIA: Russian MinFins ease in quiet trade on US holiday.</title>
<headline>Russian MinFins ease in quiet trade on US holiday.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prices of Russian MinFin bonds eased on Thursday, but dealers said the slip was due to operators staying on the sidelines on the U.S. Thanksgiving holiday.</p>
<p>		 tranche  Nov 28		  Nov 27</p>
<p> 1999 maturity (3)    83.80-84.10	   84.00-84.25</p>
<p> 2003 maturity (4)    60.65-60.95	   60.90-61.15</p>
<p> 2008 maturity (5)    42.55-42.85	   42.65-42.90</p>
<p> 2006 maturity (6)    48.80-49.10	   48.90-49.15</p>
<p> 2011 maturity (7)    36.50-36.80	   36.50-36.75</p>
<p>&quot;It is holiday in New York and operators in Europe are not active. There is nothing to talk about seriously,&quot; Most Bank dealer Alexander Rodionov said.</p>
<p>Dealers said price levels were easing, and almost no deals were struck.</p>
<p>-- Artyom Danielyan, Moscow newsroom (095) 941 8520</p>
